1
00:00:00,040 --> 00:00:03,320
[Characters, places and incidents
in this production]

2
00:00:03,320 --> 00:00:06,640
[are entirely fictitious.]

3
00:00:06,640 --> 00:00:09,960
[Viewer discretion is advised.]

4
00:00:59,838 --> 00:01:01,800
<i>You seem well-educated.</i>

5
00:01:01,800 --> 00:01:03,800
<i>You shouldn't be working as a guard.</i>

6
00:01:04,680 --> 00:01:06,320
<i>Eat lots and lots, okay?</i>

7
00:01:06,320 --> 00:01:07,650
<i>You look too thin.</i>

8
00:01:07,650 --> 00:01:08,800
<i>I am?</i>

9
00:01:08,800 --> 00:01:11,880
<i>I get off work quite late,
so I'll see you at the building tomorrow.</i>

10
00:01:11,880 --> 00:01:13,240
<i>How sweet.</i>

11
00:01:13,240 --> 00:01:15,923
<i>She is Yai's ex, you fool.</i>

12
00:01:15,923 --> 00:01:16,960
<i>What?</i>

13
00:01:16,960 --> 00:01:19,360
<i>Are you trying to rekindle an old flame?</i>

14
00:01:19,360 --> 00:01:21,400
<i>Move Daran as far as possible from my office.</i>

15
00:01:21,400 --> 00:01:24,667
<i>Don't let me see her face
or breathe the same air as her.</i>

16
00:01:24,667 --> 00:01:28,700
<i>Therefore, you can't stop me from
loving Ran, my angel, either.</i>

17
00:01:29,720 --> 00:01:31,940
The reason I want you close to me

18
00:01:33,440 --> 00:01:35,450
is so we can see each other every day.

19
00:01:38,103 --> 00:01:40,113
Maybe it'll help rekindle our old flame.

20
00:01:41,720 --> 00:01:45,231
It won't work,
because it was smothered long ago.

21
00:01:48,298 --> 00:01:49,398
Are you sure?

22
00:02:05,726 --> 00:02:08,200
You don't have time to find a rich man, do you?

23
00:02:09,080 --> 00:02:10,800
Now that I'm rich,

24
00:02:11,640 --> 00:02:13,040
are you interested?

25
00:02:14,160 --> 00:02:15,280
No, thank you.

26
00:02:16,069 --> 00:02:18,600
And you're harassing me.

27
00:02:18,600 --> 00:02:19,911
I don't like it.

28
00:02:19,911 --> 00:02:21,670
I'll report this to the foundation.

29
00:02:22,888 --> 00:02:25,280
I didn't really want to be near you,

30
00:02:25,280 --> 00:02:27,214
but since you won't quit,

31
00:02:28,880 --> 00:02:31,180
I'll make sure you see my face every day.

32
00:02:33,698 --> 00:02:36,120
Until I can't take it anymore and quit?

33
00:02:37,893 --> 00:02:39,720
I'm tougher than you think.

34
00:02:48,065 --> 00:02:49,200
Enough.

35
00:02:50,880 --> 00:02:52,000
Get out.

36
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:34,377
<i>You don't have your wealth anymore.</i>

37
00:03:34,377 --> 00:03:36,960
<i>I suppose you have nothing left for me now.</i>

38
00:03:36,960 --> 00:03:39,120
<i>I want to live comfortably</i>

39
00:03:39,120 --> 00:03:42,040
<i>with a bright future ahead of me.</i>

40
00:03:42,040 --> 00:03:43,720
<i>What are you getting at?</i>

41
00:03:44,480 --> 00:03:45,680
<i>Just say it.</i>

42
00:03:51,822 --> 00:03:53,133
<i>Let's break up.</i>

43
00:03:56,720 --> 00:04:00,425
<i>- You don't love me anymore?
- Don't be ridiculous!</i>

44
00:04:00,425 --> 00:04:02,107
<i>Or maybe just shut up.</i>

45
00:04:02,727 --> 00:04:05,160
<i>- Is it because of money?
- Yeah.</i>

46
00:04:05,160 --> 00:04:07,715
<i>Money might not be everything in life,</i>

47
00:04:07,715 --> 00:04:10,703
<i>but it can help sustain your life.</i>

48
00:04:10,703 --> 00:04:12,320
<i>If you don't have money,</i>

49
00:04:12,320 --> 00:04:14,600
<i>then it doesn't matter anymore.</i>

50
00:04:19,899 --> 00:04:21,010
<i>Fine.</i>

51
00:04:22,400 --> 00:04:25,618
<i>From now on, let's never meet again.</i>

52
00:04:27,200 --> 00:04:28,920
<i>You go your way.</i>

53
00:04:29,760 --> 00:04:31,600
<i>I go my way.</i>

54
00:04:32,440 --> 00:04:33,600
<i>If we do meet again,</i>

55
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:37,360
<i>I can't guarantee</i>

56
00:04:37,360 --> 00:04:39,360
<i>what I'll do to a woman like you!</i>

57
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:39,080
[Employment Application]
[Daran Kaewkaruna]

58
00:05:51,215 --> 00:05:53,000
Yes, Chairman?

59
00:05:53,000 --> 00:05:54,880
Get me an investigator.

60
00:06:00,880 --> 00:06:03,230
So, there will be a male host

61
00:06:03,230 --> 00:06:06,430
and a female guest,
who will talk about her first love.

62
00:06:06,430 --> 00:06:09,319
This is the overall concept of our show.

63
00:06:09,319 --> 00:06:11,630
And this is the format for our new show
[I Want to Tell You, My First Love]

64
00:06:11,630 --> 00:06:14,010
that we'll pitch to the channel next week.

65
00:06:18,167 --> 00:06:19,360
Ms. Natasha?

66
00:06:20,893 --> 00:06:23,370
We've finished our show presentation.

67
00:06:23,370 --> 00:06:25,090
We'd appreciate your feedback.

68
00:06:27,520 --> 00:06:28,760
It's pretty cute.

69
00:06:28,760 --> 00:06:30,160
Quite interesting.

70
00:06:32,060 --> 00:06:33,630
[I Want to Tell You, My First Love]

71
00:06:35,160 --> 00:06:36,720
What is the name of the show again?

72
00:06:36,720 --> 00:06:39,080
"I Want to Tell You, My First Love."

73
00:06:41,560 --> 00:06:43,410
Who came up with this name?

74
00:06:44,928 --> 00:06:46,680
Has this been discussed at all?

75
00:06:46,680 --> 00:06:48,560
"I Want to Tell You, My First Love"?

76
00:06:48,560 --> 00:06:51,240
Is everyone's first love that memorable?

77
00:06:51,240 --> 00:06:53,465
What about those who had a terrible first love?

78
00:06:53,465 --> 00:06:55,090
Who would want to watch this show?

79
00:06:55,090 --> 00:06:58,070
Do you want viewers to throw
their remotes at the screen?

80
00:06:58,070 --> 00:06:59,435
Think of something else!

81
00:07:00,840 --> 00:07:03,018
- Reschedule my meeting.
- Yes.

82
00:07:04,440 --> 00:07:06,951
[I Want to Tell You, My First Love]

83
00:07:23,840 --> 00:07:26,440
[2026]

84
00:07:26,440 --> 00:07:29,200
<i>Yai, can I sit with you?</i>
[2013]

85
00:07:30,520 --> 00:07:32,880
<i>Go ahead, there's some space.</i>

86
00:07:36,080 --> 00:07:38,510
<i>Yai, where are you going?</i>

87
00:08:01,680 --> 00:08:03,755
<i>I heard Yai is good at taking photos.</i>

88
00:08:03,755 --> 00:08:06,044
<i>Why don't you ask him to take your pictures?</i>

89
00:08:06,044 --> 00:08:08,733
<i>You can't ask him directly.</i>

90
00:08:08,733 --> 00:08:10,622
<i>If he wants to take your photos,</i>

91
00:08:10,622 --> 00:08:12,200
<i>he'll do it himself.</i>

92
00:08:12,200 --> 00:08:14,120
<i>You know him so well.</i>

93
00:08:14,120 --> 00:08:16,020
<i>Thank you.</i>
[Valentine's Day]

94
00:08:18,520 --> 00:08:20,930
<i>And to make this
a special moment for our band,</i>

95
00:08:20,930 --> 00:08:25,600
<i>we would like to invite our sweet
president to join us on stage for a song.</i>

96
00:08:25,600 --> 00:08:28,210
<i>Please welcome Daran.</i>

97
00:08:28,210 --> 00:08:29,370
<i>Daran!</i>

98
00:08:29,370 --> 00:08:30,380
<i>Daran!</i>

99
00:08:30,380 --> 00:08:32,760
<i>Daran! Daran!</i>

100
00:08:32,760 --> 00:08:34,810
<i>Come on, Ran. Let's go. Make way, please.</i>

101
00:08:34,810 --> 00:08:35,900
<i>- Make way, please.
- Daran!</i>

102
00:08:35,900 --> 00:08:37,190
<i>- Daran!
- Daran!</i>

103
00:08:37,190 --> 00:08:38,610
<i>Daran!</i>

104
00:08:38,610 --> 00:08:39,622
<i>Hey!</i>

105
00:08:41,236 --> 00:08:43,216
<i>I saw you trip my friend.</i>

106
00:08:43,216 --> 00:08:44,841
<i>Tripped her?</i>

107
00:08:44,841 --> 00:08:45,960
<i>Who did?</i>

108
00:08:45,960 --> 00:08:47,665
<i>No one saw that.</i>

109
00:08:47,665 --> 00:08:48,709
<i>Did you?</i>

110
00:08:50,440 --> 00:08:53,400
<i>- You...
- Nooch, stop.</i>

111
00:08:53,400 --> 00:08:57,360
<i>Even the sweet student president
doesn't seem to mind.</i>

112
00:08:59,800 --> 00:09:01,542
<i>But I do.</i>

113
00:09:04,880 --> 00:09:06,160
<i>Come on, Ran.</i>

114
00:09:30,720 --> 00:09:35,100
<i>♪ If you're a mountain, then I'll be a forest ♪</i>

115
00:09:35,100 --> 00:09:39,320
<i>♪ Embracing you to keep you warm in my chest ♪</i>

116
00:09:39,320 --> 00:09:43,705
<i>♪ If you're the sky, then I'll be the clouds ♪</i>

117
00:09:43,705 --> 00:09:47,465
<i>♪ Embracing you to keep you company ♪</i>

118
00:09:48,400 --> 00:09:52,465
<i>♪ If you're a car, then I'll be the roads ♪</i>

119
00:09:52,465 --> 00:09:56,760
<i>♪ If you're the Moon,
then I'll be the stars for you ♪</i>

120
00:09:56,760 --> 00:10:01,040
<i>♪ Staying by your side and giving you warmth ♪</i>

121
00:10:01,040 --> 00:10:04,740
<i>♪ Even when you're down,
I won't leave your side ♪</i>

122
00:10:24,680 --> 00:10:27,160
[Supawadee]
[Daran]

123
00:10:32,584 --> 00:10:34,178
[Daran]

124
00:10:35,600 --> 00:10:38,200
<i>You're so beautiful today!</i>

125
00:10:38,200 --> 00:10:39,510
<i>Thanks, Nooch.</i>

126
00:10:39,510 --> 00:10:41,834
<i>Next year, let me have a turn too.</i>

127
00:10:46,015 --> 00:10:47,360
<i>- Ow!
- Oh!</i>

128
00:10:47,360 --> 00:10:49,520
<i>Ran! What's wrong?</i>

129
00:10:49,520 --> 00:10:51,333
<i>There's something in my shoe.</i>

130
00:10:51,333 --> 00:10:53,210
<i>What... Wait a sec.</i>

131
00:10:54,320 --> 00:10:55,517
<i>Ran!</i>

132
00:10:55,517 --> 00:10:57,090
<i>What the hell is this?</i>

133
00:10:58,840 --> 00:11:00,710
<i>And this is an important moment</i>
[Loy Krathong Festival 2013]

134
00:11:00,710 --> 00:11:03,360
<i>when our Noppamas Queens will take the stage.</i>

135
00:11:03,360 --> 00:11:05,210
<i>Whoever you like</i>

136
00:11:05,210 --> 00:11:07,200
<i>or are secretly rooting for...</i>

137
00:11:07,200 --> 00:11:09,160
<i>Just how beautiful they'll be...</i>

138
00:11:09,160 --> 00:11:11,128
<i>You'll have to wait and see.</i>

139
00:11:11,128 --> 00:11:12,480
<i>And...</i>

140
00:11:12,480 --> 00:11:15,135
<i>- the first contestant is...
- Yai!</i>

141
00:11:15,760 --> 00:11:19,036
<i>Someone put a glass shard in Ran's shoe.
The cut is very deep.</i>

142
00:11:19,036 --> 00:11:20,886
<i>Nilapia is taking her to the hospital.</i>

143
00:11:55,602 --> 00:11:58,900
You're not the only one
who can remember your first love, Yai.

144
00:12:02,989 --> 00:12:04,764
I'll always remember mine.

145
00:12:20,360 --> 00:12:22,440
Don't worry.

146
00:12:22,440 --> 00:12:25,400
I'll take care of that woman and Yai for you.

147
00:12:25,400 --> 00:12:28,244
But right now, Grandma Namthip
is watching me closely.

148
00:12:28,244 --> 00:12:29,920
I can't do much.

149
00:12:30,920 --> 00:12:34,508
Please don't let word get out
that I asked you for help, Auntie.

150
00:12:35,408 --> 00:12:38,240
I don't want to have
any more problems with Yai.

151
00:12:38,240 --> 00:12:40,394
I won't tell anyone.

152
00:12:40,394 --> 00:12:42,200
If you're not giving up,

153
00:12:42,200 --> 00:12:43,560
I won't either.

154
00:12:45,288 --> 00:12:47,240
But do you know how she came back?

155
00:12:47,240 --> 00:12:49,320
She'd been gone for more than ten years.

156
00:12:50,360 --> 00:12:53,415
I don't know how she came back either.

157
00:12:54,640 --> 00:12:56,581
I only know that she's back now.

158
00:12:57,440 --> 00:12:58,550
Auntie,

159
00:12:59,880 --> 00:13:02,525
I don't want to lose Yai again.

160
00:13:04,106 --> 00:13:06,286
She's definitely coming back for Yai.

161
00:13:28,977 --> 00:13:31,177
[MJTV Broadcasting]

162
00:13:34,469 --> 00:13:36,880
Why is she on this floor?

163
00:13:36,880 --> 00:13:40,400
Letting her work here
is already suspicious enough,

164
00:13:40,400 --> 00:13:44,222
and now you're keeping her close, too?
How should I feel about this?

165
00:13:44,222 --> 00:13:47,890
Oh, are you planning to make up with her?

166
00:13:50,080 --> 00:13:51,800
Get her out of here!

167
00:13:53,360 --> 00:13:55,444
Tell Lek yourself then, Mom.

168
00:13:55,444 --> 00:13:57,310
He's the one organizing all of this.

169
00:14:01,792 --> 00:14:03,010
Yai,

170
00:14:03,831 --> 00:14:07,690
you're his big brother.
He'll definitely listen to you.

171
00:14:08,288 --> 00:14:11,120
Just tell Lek

172
00:14:11,120 --> 00:14:13,720
that I want her out of here!

173
00:14:16,662 --> 00:14:20,043
Even Grandma can't make Lek do it.

174
00:14:20,043 --> 00:14:22,134
What makes you think I can?

175
00:14:22,134 --> 00:14:24,093
You tell him yourself, Mom.

176
00:14:24,093 --> 00:14:27,336
If he were my son, I would've
already told him that!

177
00:14:27,336 --> 00:14:31,654
And what... what will you do
if Nana finds out? Huh?

178
00:14:31,654 --> 00:14:33,582
Is that all you have to say to me?

179
00:14:33,582 --> 00:14:36,131
I have a meeting with
the programming department. Excuse me.

180
00:14:36,131 --> 00:14:37,623
Yai.

181
00:14:37,623 --> 00:14:38,889
Yai!

182
00:14:40,400 --> 00:14:42,777
I have a meeting. Please excuse me.

183
00:14:43,480 --> 00:14:45,120
Yai!

184
00:14:45,120 --> 00:14:46,520
Yai!

185
00:15:29,920 --> 00:15:31,200
I'm going down.

186
00:15:41,440 --> 00:15:44,600
Don't you dare do what I think you'll do.

187
00:15:45,440 --> 00:15:47,120
Otherwise,

188
00:15:47,920 --> 00:15:51,308
I'll make sure there's no place
for you in society

189
00:15:52,238 --> 00:15:55,990
and no chance of
ever getting back on your feet.

190
00:16:01,437 --> 00:16:05,530
Did you hear what Mrs. Angkhana said
to Mr. Alex's angel, Dad?

191
00:16:06,320 --> 00:16:08,520
It looks like she was speaking.

192
00:16:08,520 --> 00:16:12,350
Maybe she caught a cold
and couldn't breathe through her nose,

193
00:16:12,350 --> 00:16:14,311
so she breathed through her mouth.

194
00:16:14,311 --> 00:16:17,066
No. I think she definitely said something.

195
00:16:17,766 --> 00:16:20,280
Mr. Alex said that Mrs. Angkhana despises Ran.

196
00:16:20,280 --> 00:16:22,565
Or is it a death threat?

197
00:16:22,565 --> 00:16:23,866
Are you crazy?

198
00:16:23,866 --> 00:16:25,450
Who would just murder someone?

199
00:16:25,450 --> 00:16:27,760
- We live in a country with laws! Damn...
- Uncle.

200
00:16:27,760 --> 00:16:28,977
Yes?

201
00:16:28,977 --> 00:16:33,080
Please make sure all the cameras
record sound clearly. All of them.

202
00:16:33,080 --> 00:16:36,880
I think there's a flaw in our security system.

203
00:16:37,640 --> 00:16:38,946
Yes.

204
00:16:39,977 --> 00:16:41,422
It's almost lunchtime.

205
00:16:41,422 --> 00:16:44,080
I'll go get the food so Ran can eat on time.

206
00:16:44,080 --> 00:16:45,290
Yes, yes, alright.

207
00:16:53,358 --> 00:16:55,720
<i>Hey, birdbrain, did you hear what I just said?</i>

208
00:16:55,720 --> 00:16:56,880
[2026]

209
00:16:56,880 --> 00:16:58,030
[2013]

210
00:16:58,030 --> 00:16:59,066
<i>Hey!</i>

211
00:17:00,040 --> 00:17:02,080
<i>I said, give me your money. Hurry!</i>

212
00:17:07,480 --> 00:17:08,740
<i>100 baht?</i>

213
00:17:08,740 --> 00:17:09,977
<i>Are you shitting me?</i>

214
00:17:09,977 --> 00:17:11,466
<i>Your family is so fucking rich,</i>

215
00:17:11,466 --> 00:17:13,640
<i>but they only gave you
this much pocket money?</i>

216
00:17:13,640 --> 00:17:15,311
<i>Search him!</i>

217
00:17:15,311 --> 00:17:16,360
<i>Hey!</i>

218
00:17:17,680 --> 00:17:19,600
<i>Hey, it's empty!</i>

219
00:17:21,320 --> 00:17:24,340
<i>Tomorrow, you have to bring me
another 500. Got it?</i>

220
00:17:25,449 --> 00:17:26,960
<i>Grandma wouldn't give me that much.</i>

221
00:17:26,960 --> 00:17:30,240
<i>You're so loyal to your grandma,
are you a dog or something?</i>

222
00:17:30,240 --> 00:17:31,920
<i>Hey, but I think he is.</i>

223
00:17:31,920 --> 00:17:34,145
<i>Hey! How does a dog walk?</i>

224
00:17:34,145 --> 00:17:35,425
<i>Show me!</i>

225
00:17:36,920 --> 00:17:38,160
<i>Hey!</i>

226
00:17:38,880 --> 00:17:40,480
<i>I told you to get on all fours.</i>

227
00:17:45,320 --> 00:17:46,480
<i>Yai.</i>

228
00:17:49,840 --> 00:17:51,840
<i>Isn't that Lek, your younger brother?</i>

229
00:17:59,733 --> 00:18:01,040
<i>Bark, too!</i>

230
00:18:01,040 --> 00:18:02,160
<i>Louder!</i>

231
00:18:03,390 --> 00:18:04,470
<i>Yai!</i>

232
00:18:06,925 --> 00:18:08,240
<i>Keep barking!</i>

233
00:18:08,240 --> 00:18:08,900
<i>Woof, woof.</i>

234
00:18:08,900 --> 00:18:10,400
<i>Bark louder!</i>

235
00:18:10,400 --> 00:18:12,851
<i>- Louder.
- Woof, woof.</i>

236
00:18:13,830 --> 00:18:15,610
<i>Circle!</i>

237
00:18:15,610 --> 00:18:16,711
<i>Circle, circle.</i>

238
00:18:16,711 --> 00:18:17,900
<i>- Crawl in a circle!
- Bark, too!</i>

239
00:18:17,900 --> 00:18:20,533
<i>- Bark!
- Holy shit, it really works.</i>

240
00:18:32,332 --> 00:18:33,444
<i>Lek.</i>

241
00:18:35,059 --> 00:18:37,777
<i>You have to learn to
defend yourself at school.</i>

242
00:18:39,377 --> 00:18:41,711
<i>I can't always be there to help you.</i>

243
00:18:41,711 --> 00:18:44,410
<i>You have to stand up for yourself.</i>

244
00:18:44,410 --> 00:18:45,555
<i>Understand?</i>

245
00:18:57,491 --> 00:18:58,733
<i>Yai!</i>

246
00:19:00,757 --> 00:19:02,310
<i>We won't be here next year.</i>

247
00:19:03,240 --> 00:19:05,320
<i>He has to handle them himself.</i>

248
00:19:05,320 --> 00:19:07,296
<i>But I feel bad for him!</i>

249
00:19:11,569 --> 00:19:14,347
<i>Hey, come to me! Quick!</i>

250
00:19:18,898 --> 00:19:20,600
<i>- Hey!
- Bark!</i>

251
00:19:22,960 --> 00:19:25,450
<i>You know I do taekwondo, yeah?</i>

252
00:19:26,120 --> 00:19:28,480
<i>- What do we do...
- You wanna mess with me, huh?</i>

253
00:19:29,800 --> 00:19:30,810
<i>What should we do?</i>

254
00:19:30,810 --> 00:19:32,700
<i>Hey! Go, go!</i>

255
00:19:40,360 --> 00:19:41,800
<i>You're safe now.</i>

256
00:19:45,313 --> 00:19:47,200
<i>Does it hurt a lot?</i>

257
00:19:47,200 --> 00:19:48,320
<i>Let me see.</i>

258
00:19:52,090 --> 00:19:53,310
<i>Let me...</i>

259
00:20:18,463 --> 00:20:19,600
<i>Lek...</i>

260
00:20:41,734 --> 00:20:44,920
<i>The library is for reading books.</i>

261
00:20:44,920 --> 00:20:47,720
<i>No one comes here to sit and cry.</i>

262
00:20:53,891 --> 00:20:57,710
<i>Since you're here,
why don't you try reading a book?</i>

263
00:21:29,529 --> 00:21:31,330
<i>Do you know this book,</i>

264
00:21:31,330 --> 00:21:32,010
[A Prince's Heart]

265
00:21:32,010 --> 00:21:33,470
<i>"A Prince's Heart"?</i>

266
00:21:34,035 --> 00:21:35,765
<i>I love reading it so much,</i>

267
00:21:35,765 --> 00:21:37,160
<i>I read it, like,</i>

268
00:21:37,160 --> 00:21:38,680
<i>more than ten times.</i>

269
00:21:49,240 --> 00:21:50,880
<i>Each time,</i>

270
00:21:50,880 --> 00:21:53,400
<i>I learned a new lesson from the book.</i>

271
00:21:53,400 --> 00:21:57,130
<i>Do you know what I learned
the first time I read it?</i>

272
00:22:00,287 --> 00:22:03,160
<i>"What is essential cannot
be seen with the eye.</i>

273
00:22:03,160 --> 00:22:05,440
<i>It can only be seen with the heart."</i>

274
00:22:05,440 --> 00:22:07,440
<i>Although the prince is unsightly,</i>

275
00:22:07,440 --> 00:22:11,285
<i>his true value lies not in his appearance,</i>

276
00:22:11,285 --> 00:22:12,910
<i>but in his character,</i>

277
00:22:12,910 --> 00:22:15,420
<i>behavior, and attitude.</i>

278
00:22:19,039 --> 00:22:20,959
<i>Do you understand what I mean?</i>

279
00:22:26,677 --> 00:22:29,710
<i>Even though they were mean to you today,</i>

280
00:22:31,100 --> 00:22:34,000
<i>that doesn't mean you're worthless.</i>

281
00:22:34,000 --> 00:22:37,445
<i>Yai told me that your grandma loves you a lot,</i>

282
00:22:37,445 --> 00:22:40,482
<i>and he only wants what's best for you.</i>

283
00:22:40,482 --> 00:22:43,925
<i>That means you're important to your family.</i>

284
00:22:44,710 --> 00:22:46,280
<i>If it were me,</i>

285
00:22:46,280 --> 00:22:48,920
<i>I'd only care about my family, who love me,</i>

286
00:22:48,920 --> 00:22:52,735
<i>and ignore people like the ones</i>

287
00:22:52,735 --> 00:22:54,960
<i>who picked on you.</i>

288
00:22:54,960 --> 00:22:57,300
<i>Because they're not worth it to me.</i>

289
00:23:03,111 --> 00:23:04,780
<i>Give it a read.</i>

290
00:23:07,483 --> 00:23:10,731
<i>Then come tell me what you learned from it.</i>

291
00:23:10,731 --> 00:23:13,643
<i>Maybe we'll think the same thing.</i>
[A Prince's Heart]

292
00:23:13,643 --> 00:23:16,058
<i>But even if we don't, that's okay.</i>

293
00:23:16,058 --> 00:23:18,384
<i>We can exchange ideas that way.</i>

294
00:23:18,384 --> 00:23:19,873
<i>It helps sharpen your mind.</i>

295
00:23:30,330 --> 00:23:31,590
<i>Ran!</i>

296
00:23:31,590 --> 00:23:33,550
<i>The horse taught me how taming</i>

297
00:23:33,550 --> 00:23:35,140
<i>is like building a bond</i>

298
00:23:35,140 --> 00:23:39,390
<i>that makes someone
the one who's special only to you.</i>

299
00:24:04,912 --> 00:24:06,429
<i>Teacher, help!</i>

300
00:24:06,429 --> 00:24:07,600
<i>Teacher!</i>

301
00:24:07,600 --> 00:24:09,040
<i>- Teacher!
- Run!</i>

302
00:24:19,080 --> 00:24:23,393
<i>Time is the most precious gift,
because it's limited.</i>

303
00:24:23,393 --> 00:24:25,440
<i>If you spend time on something,</i>

304
00:24:25,440 --> 00:24:27,880
<i>it becomes precious to you.</i>

305
00:24:27,880 --> 00:24:29,380
<i>Just as the prince in the story</i>

306
00:24:29,380 --> 00:24:32,299
<i>devotes his time to saving his dying foal,</i>

307
00:24:32,299 --> 00:24:36,720
<i>helping it survive and
grow into a beautiful, majestic horse!</i>

308
00:24:46,960 --> 00:24:49,670
[Valentine's Day]

309
00:24:51,200 --> 00:24:54,670
<i>♪ I won't let anything bring you harm ♪</i>

310
00:24:55,760 --> 00:25:00,355
<i>♪ As long as I'm right here ♪</i>

311
00:25:00,355 --> 00:25:04,129
<i>♪ I'll love you with all my heart, dear ♪</i>

312
00:25:05,320 --> 00:25:11,283
<i>♪ Baby, I love you ♪</i>

313
00:25:15,760 --> 00:25:17,943
[2013]

314
00:25:19,880 --> 00:25:22,200
[2026]

315
00:25:31,000 --> 00:25:32,090
Ran.

316
00:25:34,120 --> 00:25:35,240
Let's eat.

317
00:25:38,720 --> 00:25:40,400
I'm not hungry.

318
00:25:40,400 --> 00:25:41,479
Did the Chairman

319
00:25:42,040 --> 00:25:43,480
say something to you?

320
00:25:48,600 --> 00:25:50,040
Are you alright?

321
00:25:51,640 --> 00:25:53,800
It looks like you don't want
to be on that floor.

322
00:25:55,088 --> 00:25:57,210
I'm just doing my part.

323
00:25:57,911 --> 00:25:59,500
It's nothing I can't handle.

324
00:26:00,480 --> 00:26:02,089
No need to worry about me, Alex.

325
00:26:03,310 --> 00:26:04,410
I'm fine.

326
00:26:09,284 --> 00:26:10,920
I'm hungry.

327
00:26:10,920 --> 00:26:14,200
Let's eat so we can get back to work.

328
00:26:17,022 --> 00:26:18,520
That's great.

329
00:26:18,520 --> 00:26:21,600
Eat up so you'll have the energy to work.

330
00:26:21,600 --> 00:26:22,600
Thanks.

331
00:26:34,273 --> 00:26:36,090
You don't have to pass me food.

332
00:26:37,520 --> 00:26:38,720
Just eat.

333
00:26:45,859 --> 00:26:47,010
Why are you here?

334
00:26:47,644 --> 00:26:49,420
Well, I'm here to see my zombie girl.

335
00:26:49,420 --> 00:26:51,955
See? I bought her some food.

336
00:26:55,171 --> 00:26:57,915
- Hey, Yai!
- I'll eat it.

337
00:26:57,915 --> 00:26:59,590
You can't!

338
00:26:59,590 --> 00:27:02,133
I had to book way ahead to get this.

339
00:27:12,859 --> 00:27:15,100
She's in front of Yai's office?

340
00:27:20,078 --> 00:27:21,168
Yes.

341
00:27:22,440 --> 00:27:25,000
Thank you for telling me this.

342
00:27:41,849 --> 00:27:43,110
Hello.

343
00:27:44,080 --> 00:27:45,920
I think Yai

344
00:27:46,688 --> 00:27:50,600
is trying to rekindle an old flame, Sam.

345
00:27:50,600 --> 00:27:51,920
No wonder.

346
00:28:26,785 --> 00:28:28,620
Where are they?

347
00:28:38,770 --> 00:28:40,310
There's no one here.

348
00:28:41,955 --> 00:28:43,090
Come in.

349
00:28:47,017 --> 00:28:48,960
Thanks, Ran.

350
00:28:48,960 --> 00:28:50,040
Come.

351
00:29:05,720 --> 00:29:07,960
- I'm sorry.
- Don't.

352
00:29:07,960 --> 00:29:10,182
Whoever put them there can pick them up.

353
00:30:37,280 --> 00:30:39,070
[Executive Chairman]

354
00:30:39,070 --> 00:30:40,200
- Hey.
- Hey!

355
00:30:40,200 --> 00:30:42,333
Hey! Ow!!

356
00:30:49,466 --> 00:30:50,688
I'm sorry.

357
00:30:50,688 --> 00:30:51,780
Daran.

358
00:30:54,060 --> 00:30:56,720
Who said you could get violent with our artist?

359
00:30:58,000 --> 00:30:59,711
It's my fault.

360
00:30:59,711 --> 00:31:01,400
Don't blame Daran.

361
00:31:02,000 --> 00:31:05,040
She made it clear
I shouldn't get within a meter of her,

362
00:31:05,040 --> 00:31:06,560
or she'll kick me in the neck.

363
00:31:06,560 --> 00:31:08,880
Why didn't you do that, then?
That wasn't enough!

364
00:31:12,288 --> 00:31:13,800
I mean...

365
00:31:13,800 --> 00:31:17,954
You threatened to kick our artist
in the neck and assaulted him.

366
00:31:17,954 --> 00:31:19,834
I'll have to punish you severely.

367
00:31:21,640 --> 00:31:24,305
I told you this is my fault!

368
00:31:24,305 --> 00:31:25,990
Be quiet.

369
00:31:25,990 --> 00:31:27,995
How could I do that?

370
00:31:27,995 --> 00:31:29,195
"Be quiet"?

371
00:31:29,977 --> 00:31:33,280
Do you really think that I don't know?

372
00:31:33,280 --> 00:31:35,169
You still love Daran, don't you?

373
00:31:37,246 --> 00:31:38,661
But you won't admit it,

374
00:31:38,661 --> 00:31:40,676
so you put her outside your room.

375
00:31:41,810 --> 00:31:43,310
You're acting tough nowadays.

376
00:31:43,310 --> 00:31:45,377
If you were truly indifferent toward her,

377
00:31:45,377 --> 00:31:47,500
you wouldn't be doing all of this.

378
00:31:47,500 --> 00:31:49,910
I know you well enough, you hypocrite.

379
00:31:49,910 --> 00:31:52,977
- Sam!
- Yes, sir?

380
00:31:52,977 --> 00:31:56,887
Are you going to punish me?
Do it quickly, so I can leave.

381
00:31:56,887 --> 00:31:58,244
Get out.

382
00:31:58,888 --> 00:32:00,820
There won't be any punishment.

383
00:32:00,820 --> 00:32:02,720
I won't let emotions affect my work.

384
00:32:02,720 --> 00:32:04,555
- Sam's at fault this time.
- Yes.

385
00:32:04,555 --> 00:32:06,010
It's my fault.

386
00:32:08,000 --> 00:32:09,134
Yes.

387
00:32:14,197 --> 00:32:16,055
You can't seem to shut up, can you?

388
00:32:16,055 --> 00:32:17,181
Am I wrong, then?

389
00:32:17,181 --> 00:32:18,910
Have I ever seen you date anyone?

390
00:32:19,840 --> 00:32:23,120
There's only Nana, who forced
you to get engaged to her.

391
00:32:23,120 --> 00:32:27,888
And you don't seem to be
all that fond of Nana, either.

392
00:32:27,888 --> 00:32:29,880
She's the only one who chased after you.

393
00:32:30,598 --> 00:32:32,880
Or is it that...

394
00:32:35,400 --> 00:32:38,440
- you still haven't moved on from Daran--
- I already did.

395
00:32:38,440 --> 00:32:42,280
You're misunderstanding me, and
you made her misunderstand me, too.

396
00:32:42,280 --> 00:32:43,720
Go set her straight.

397
00:32:43,720 --> 00:32:45,010
Does this mean...

398
00:32:45,720 --> 00:32:47,360
I can flirt with Daran?

399
00:32:47,360 --> 00:32:50,160
- You can't!
- Why not?

400
00:32:50,160 --> 00:32:50,940
Well...

401
00:32:52,610 --> 00:32:53,666
Why can't I?

402
00:32:53,666 --> 00:32:55,120
Because the contract says...

403
00:32:56,000 --> 00:33:00,054
"Romantic relationships
with employees are prohibited." It's a rule.

404
00:33:00,054 --> 00:33:01,520
Not even the security guards?

405
00:33:01,520 --> 00:33:02,520
No!

406
00:33:04,320 --> 00:33:06,840
I'm asking you, Sam. Leave Daran alone.

407
00:33:06,840 --> 00:33:11,760
Although I hate her, I just can't hand her over
to a womanizer like you.

408
00:33:11,760 --> 00:33:12,920
Find someone else.

409
00:33:16,252 --> 00:33:17,840
Then, how about this?

410
00:33:18,760 --> 00:33:20,360
I have...

411
00:33:20,360 --> 00:33:22,844
a great offer for you to choose from.

412
00:33:22,844 --> 00:33:24,040
Between...

413
00:33:24,040 --> 00:33:25,640
Option one,

414
00:33:25,640 --> 00:33:28,480
I'll try to change myself.

415
00:33:28,480 --> 00:33:29,777
Option two,

416
00:33:29,777 --> 00:33:32,688
I'll convince Daran to quit her job

417
00:33:32,688 --> 00:33:35,856
so that I can flirt with her.

418
00:33:35,856 --> 00:33:37,440
Which one will you choose?

419
00:33:37,440 --> 00:33:39,498
I have a third option for you.

420
00:33:39,498 --> 00:33:41,488
- What is it?
- This!

421
00:33:41,488 --> 00:33:43,710
- Something like this!
- Ow! Yai!

422
00:33:43,710 --> 00:33:45,733
Aren't you forgetting a rule?

423
00:33:45,733 --> 00:33:47,576
"Violence against artists is prohibited."

424
00:33:47,576 --> 00:33:49,080
Aren't you forgetting...

425
00:33:49,680 --> 00:33:51,560
That I'm the owner of this company?

426
00:33:54,340 --> 00:33:57,200
- I won't forget.
- Go clear this up.

427
00:33:58,520 --> 00:34:00,129
Okay, I'll go.

428
00:34:05,160 --> 00:34:07,449
Daran!

429
00:34:13,080 --> 00:34:16,600
I was mistaken about Yai
and spoke without thinking.

430
00:34:17,520 --> 00:34:21,120
I'm here to tell you
that what I said wasn't true.

431
00:34:22,440 --> 00:34:23,560
Yes.

432
00:34:25,911 --> 00:34:28,560
I don't want to head down yet...

433
00:34:31,266 --> 00:34:33,880
If you don't stop flirting with me,

434
00:34:33,880 --> 00:34:37,440
I'll pretend you don't exist
and ignore you completely.

435
00:34:37,440 --> 00:34:39,116
What a meanie.

436
00:34:42,720 --> 00:34:43,960
My arm hurts.

437
00:34:43,960 --> 00:34:46,000
Ow! My leg hurts.

438
00:34:46,000 --> 00:34:47,855
Ow! My heart hurts.

439
00:34:49,320 --> 00:34:50,680
I can't get back up.

440
00:34:51,360 --> 00:34:52,680
Can you help me up?

441
00:34:57,710 --> 00:34:58,900
It's here.

442
00:35:00,694 --> 00:35:02,400
So cold.

443
00:35:16,711 --> 00:35:18,466
Those two still love each other.

444
00:35:22,431 --> 00:35:23,800
You're home.

445
00:35:37,880 --> 00:35:39,640
[Dao]

446
00:35:40,560 --> 00:35:41,920
What is it, Dao?

447
00:35:50,684 --> 00:35:52,490
Whoa.

448
00:35:52,490 --> 00:35:54,400
Your room looks amazing.

449
00:35:55,680 --> 00:35:57,727
- Hello.
- Yes.

450
00:35:57,727 --> 00:35:59,330
Come eat with us.

451
00:35:59,330 --> 00:36:00,730
It's freshly cooked.

452
00:36:03,155 --> 00:36:04,730
Sorry to trouble you, Alex.

453
00:36:04,730 --> 00:36:06,640
Dao lost her wallet,

454
00:36:06,640 --> 00:36:09,357
so she only had enough
for the fare from tutoring to here.

455
00:36:09,357 --> 00:36:12,822
It's pretty late now,
and I don't want her to go home by herself,

456
00:36:12,822 --> 00:36:15,520
so I'll have her stay here tonight.

457
00:36:16,550 --> 00:36:19,400
No problem.

458
00:36:19,400 --> 00:36:20,755
Make yourself at home, Dao.

459
00:36:21,555 --> 00:36:23,733
It's a good thing. Ran won't be lonely,

460
00:36:23,733 --> 00:36:26,400
since I go out and play music every night,

461
00:36:26,400 --> 00:36:27,933
so she's usually here alone.

462
00:36:27,933 --> 00:36:31,066
She never watches TV. She just sleeps.

463
00:36:31,644 --> 00:36:33,622
How did you know I never turned it on?

464
00:36:34,560 --> 00:36:37,520
Well, everything was in the exact same place.

465
00:36:37,520 --> 00:36:39,000
The remote...

466
00:36:39,000 --> 00:36:41,002
Everything's exactly where it was.

467
00:36:41,002 --> 00:36:42,920
If Ran hadn't told me you were gay,

468
00:36:42,920 --> 00:36:45,145
I would've thought you
had feelings for my sister

469
00:36:45,145 --> 00:36:46,682
since you're this caring.

470
00:36:50,314 --> 00:36:52,091
Come, come. Let's eat.

471
00:37:01,594 --> 00:37:03,533
Don't tell me you're giving up?

472
00:37:05,688 --> 00:37:06,910
Maybe.

473
00:37:07,840 --> 00:37:12,600
But for me, I like Daran. She's driven.

474
00:37:12,600 --> 00:37:15,517
Maybe... I might continue.

475
00:37:15,517 --> 00:37:18,010
Maybe... we might stay as friends.

476
00:37:19,920 --> 00:37:22,200
Hey! What's wrong with you?

477
00:37:23,760 --> 00:37:26,400
I despise everyone who likes her.

478
00:37:26,400 --> 00:37:28,310
That means you hate Yai, too.

479
00:37:28,310 --> 00:37:31,720
It's not fair if you only hate me.

480
00:37:31,720 --> 00:37:35,680
I hate everyone who likes that woman!

481
00:37:36,622 --> 00:37:41,453
People who like her are brainless,
tasteless, and inadequate!

482
00:37:50,080 --> 00:37:52,480
She wanted me to be a third wheel

483
00:37:52,480 --> 00:37:54,558
because she's too afraid to be possessive?

484
00:37:56,080 --> 00:37:58,305
That's not going to work.

485
00:37:58,305 --> 00:37:59,575
What a nag!

486
00:38:08,088 --> 00:38:09,720
Hello, Kaew.

487
00:38:09,720 --> 00:38:12,600
Which MJTV studio did we keep the props

488
00:38:12,600 --> 00:38:14,240
for the TV shows in again?

489
00:38:15,280 --> 00:38:16,760
Thanks.

490
00:38:20,960 --> 00:38:24,080
I'll send Dao home tomorrow
once the traffic dies down, Mom.

491
00:38:25,080 --> 00:38:26,911
I'm alright.

492
00:38:26,911 --> 00:38:30,000
Work has never been easier.

493
00:38:30,000 --> 00:38:31,280
Don't worry, alright?

494
00:38:32,440 --> 00:38:34,240
Is Danai home yet?

495
00:38:36,240 --> 00:38:38,120
Are you alright by yourself?

496
00:38:39,800 --> 00:38:42,244
Okay. Alright, goodbye.

497
00:38:46,388 --> 00:38:49,977
Why can't I get the same answer as the key?

498
00:38:51,066 --> 00:38:52,488
Here.

499
00:38:52,488 --> 00:38:53,800
Let me see.

500
00:38:54,840 --> 00:38:58,120
It's been over ten years.
Do you still remember this?

501
00:38:58,120 --> 00:39:02,007
"Boy A started at the starting point
and walked 5 meters east,

502
00:39:02,007 --> 00:39:04,392
then walked 3 meters back west.

503
00:39:04,392 --> 00:39:06,692
Find the distance and displacement."

504
00:39:07,720 --> 00:39:11,640
This is quality stuff.
No wonder you've filled out.

505
00:39:12,482 --> 00:39:16,600
You haven't been here for long,
but you've gotten prettier. Did you know?

506
00:39:17,360 --> 00:39:20,060
Did you know? I'm focusing.

507
00:39:21,076 --> 00:39:22,300
Fine, I'll be quiet.

508
00:39:24,133 --> 00:39:25,500
Here.

509
00:39:25,500 --> 00:39:26,955
First, you have to understand

510
00:39:26,955 --> 00:39:30,690
that distance is the total length
of the path traveled.

511
00:39:33,280 --> 00:39:35,030
That equals...?

512
00:39:35,030 --> 00:39:36,910
Five plus three is eight.

513
00:39:36,910 --> 00:39:38,510
Yes. That's correct.

514
00:39:38,510 --> 00:39:40,560
And the displacement equals...?

515
00:39:41,400 --> 00:39:42,488
It equals...

516
00:39:43,720 --> 00:39:46,040
From the final point to the initial point.

517
00:39:47,244 --> 00:39:48,240
And?

518
00:39:48,960 --> 00:39:50,880
Five minus three equals two.

519
00:39:50,880 --> 00:39:53,230
And what did you answer?

520
00:39:53,230 --> 00:39:54,488
Three.

521
00:39:54,488 --> 00:39:55,720
Change it then.

522
00:39:58,520 --> 00:40:00,640
You're really good at this.

523
00:40:00,640 --> 00:40:03,835
Mom said that back then, you were really smart.

524
00:40:03,835 --> 00:40:05,675
I finally believe her now.

525
00:40:07,735 --> 00:40:11,379
Well, I can remember a bit,
but I'm just guessing here.

526
00:40:11,960 --> 00:40:14,076
Why didn't you pursue higher education?

527
00:40:14,076 --> 00:40:15,440
Because if you had,

528
00:40:15,440 --> 00:40:18,050
you wouldn't have to work this hard.

529
00:40:18,880 --> 00:40:19,880
Because...

530
00:40:21,155 --> 00:40:24,320
I wanted to protect
something I love as best as I could.

531
00:40:26,000 --> 00:40:29,090
To protect what I love,

532
00:40:29,090 --> 00:40:30,960
even if it means giving up everything

533
00:40:30,960 --> 00:40:33,040
and losing all I have in this world,

534
00:40:33,040 --> 00:40:34,411
I'm willing to do it.

535
00:40:34,411 --> 00:40:36,021
I wonder what that is.

536
00:40:45,640 --> 00:40:49,920
[Mr. Danai Kaewkaruna]
[Ms. Daranee Kaewkaruna]

537
00:40:49,920 --> 00:40:52,960
"Daranee Kaewkaruna..."

538
00:41:52,340 --> 00:41:55,500
Ran, I'm thirsty. I'll be right back.

539
00:42:03,720 --> 00:42:05,000
What?

540
00:42:05,000 --> 00:42:07,440
50 baht per garland?

541
00:42:07,440 --> 00:42:09,040
How is that worth the effort?

542
00:42:09,040 --> 00:42:12,124
It's all worth it.
Ran does all kinds of side hustles.

543
00:42:12,124 --> 00:42:14,498
My sister will do anything to make money.

544
00:42:18,794 --> 00:42:20,640
Are you really gay?

545
00:42:23,120 --> 00:42:24,560
You probably are.

546
00:42:24,560 --> 00:42:26,895
Otherwise, Ran wouldn't be staying with you.

547
00:42:28,640 --> 00:42:30,400
Keep that a secret

548
00:42:31,068 --> 00:42:32,520
and don't tell anyone, okay?

549
00:42:32,520 --> 00:42:35,609
Okay. So do you have a boyfriend?

550
00:42:37,043 --> 00:42:38,318
Do I have to answer?

551
00:42:38,318 --> 00:42:40,488
If you don't want to answer, that's okay.

552
00:42:41,598 --> 00:42:43,613
Then I won't.

553
00:42:43,613 --> 00:42:44,971
Okay, let's change the topic.

554
00:42:44,971 --> 00:42:47,749
Since you work as a security guard,
you get to meet Sam, right?

555
00:42:49,100 --> 00:42:50,600
Sometimes.

556
00:42:50,600 --> 00:42:51,560
Then...

557
00:42:51,560 --> 00:42:53,600
If Sam comes to work, can you let me know?

558
00:42:53,600 --> 00:42:55,080
Come on, let's exchange contacts.

559
00:42:57,040 --> 00:42:58,480
Please?

560
00:43:04,755 --> 00:43:07,355
What about you? What do you have to offer?

561
00:43:08,080 --> 00:43:10,100
What do you want, then?

562
00:43:16,920 --> 00:43:21,280
<i>♪ If you're the sky, then I'll be the clouds ♪</i>

563
00:43:21,280 --> 00:43:24,960
<i>♪ Embracing you to keep you company ♪</i>

564
00:43:25,720 --> 00:43:30,657
<i>♪ If you're a car, then I'll be the roads ♪</i>

565
00:43:30,657 --> 00:43:31,590
Come here, quick!

566
00:43:31,590 --> 00:43:34,720
<i>♪ If you're the Moon,
then I'll be the stars for you ♪</i>

567
00:43:34,720 --> 00:43:39,220
<i>♪ Staying by your side and giving you warmth ♪</i>

568
00:43:39,220 --> 00:43:42,640
<i>♪ Even when you're down,
I won't leave your side ♪</i>

569
00:43:43,960 --> 00:43:51,320
<i>♪ You're a gift sent from heaven ♪</i>

570
00:43:52,680 --> 00:44:00,255
<i>♪ I'll cherish this blessing forevermore ♪</i>

571
00:44:00,255 --> 00:44:04,130
<i>♪ I won't let anything bring you harm ♪</i>

572
00:44:04,130 --> 00:44:08,595
<i>♪ As long as I'm right here ♪</i>

573
00:44:08,595 --> 00:44:11,915
<i>♪ I'll love you with all my heart, dear ♪</i>

574
00:44:12,520 --> 00:44:15,080
<i>♪ Baby, I love you ♪</i>

575
00:44:17,022 --> 00:44:19,662
<i>♪ Baby, I love you ♪</i>

576
00:44:21,557 --> 00:44:25,688
What kind of security guards are you
to let our belongings go missing?

577
00:44:26,377 --> 00:44:27,600
Thawin.

578
00:44:27,600 --> 00:44:29,555
Answer her. She's asking you.

579
00:44:29,555 --> 00:44:31,280
I'm asking you, Uncle.

580
00:44:31,280 --> 00:44:33,430
- Well...
- Are there any security cameras?

581
00:44:33,430 --> 00:44:35,040
So I can see who took them.

582
00:44:35,040 --> 00:44:36,220
Well...

583
00:44:36,220 --> 00:44:38,955
This studio has cameras,

584
00:44:38,955 --> 00:44:42,114
but... they're not working right now.

585
00:44:42,114 --> 00:44:44,904
They were still working fine a few days ago.

586
00:44:44,904 --> 00:44:46,269
What's all this fuss about?

587
00:44:48,680 --> 00:44:50,720
The props we kept here
for our TV shows are gone.

588
00:44:50,720 --> 00:44:53,320
And there's no security camera footage.

589
00:44:53,320 --> 00:44:55,640
How am I supposed to find the culprit?

590
00:44:55,640 --> 00:44:57,080
Whose shift was it?

591
00:44:57,080 --> 00:44:58,200
Mine.

592
00:44:58,960 --> 00:45:00,130
Did you fall asleep?

593
00:45:00,130 --> 00:45:03,844
No, I didn't. But I went to the toilet.

594
00:45:03,844 --> 00:45:05,330
Oh, I remember now.

595
00:45:05,330 --> 00:45:08,560
I saw someone running out of the studio
when I came back from the toilet.

596
00:45:08,560 --> 00:45:10,760
Hey, why didn't you tell me that earlier?

597
00:45:10,760 --> 00:45:12,480
Well, I thought it was a ghost.

598
00:45:12,480 --> 00:45:14,880
Thinking it through, it's definitely a person.

599
00:45:14,880 --> 00:45:16,940
They're about this tall.

600
00:45:16,940 --> 00:45:19,220
They have a small build and a ponytail.

601
00:45:19,220 --> 00:45:21,133
They looked like...

602
00:45:21,133 --> 00:45:22,200
Daran.

603
00:45:31,916 --> 00:45:33,955
<i>Don't give me that look.</i>

604
00:45:33,955 --> 00:45:35,430
<i>Stop bothering Daran already.</i>

605
00:45:35,430 --> 00:45:38,488
<i>I won't back down as easily as before.</i>

606
00:45:38,488 --> 00:45:39,972
<i>Do you want to come live with me?</i>

607
00:45:39,972 --> 00:45:41,933
<i>I don't see you as a toy.</i>

608
00:45:41,933 --> 00:45:42,960
<i>Whoa!</i>

609
00:45:42,960 --> 00:45:45,640
<i>Do you understand
how it feels to be fooled now?</i>

610
00:45:45,640 --> 00:45:48,075
<i>- How did you turn out like this?
- Ran. Ran!</i>

611
00:45:48,075 --> 00:45:49,645
<i>For you to help her this much,</i>

612
00:45:49,645 --> 00:45:51,315
<i>how many times have you slept with her?</i>

613
00:45:51,315 --> 00:45:53,600
<i>- Are you trying to seduce Lek?
- Huh?</i>

614
00:45:53,600 --> 00:45:54,760
<i>Aren't you two in love?</i>

615
00:45:54,760 --> 00:45:56,960
<i>Move everything here to the wall over there.</i>

616
00:45:58,588 --> 00:46:02,361
<i>Wasn't it all because of you
that we ended up like this?</i>
